h3>Egyptian</h3><p><b>Symbol</b></p><ol><li>Biliteral phonogram for <b>ẖn</b>.</li></ol></html><h3>Egyptian</h3><p><b>Symbol</b></p><ol><li>Biliteral phonogram for <b>nj</b>, especially in <i>nn</i> (“not”).</li><li>Uniliteral phonogram for <b>n</b>, especially in <i>nn</i> (“not”).</li><li>Ideogram for <i>nj</i> (“not”).</li><li>Phonogram for <b>jw</b> or <b>jwt</b> in <i>jwt</i> (“that not”) and <i>jwtj</i> (“which not”).</li><li>Determinative sign marking negation.</li></ol></html><h3>Egyptian</h3><p><b>Symbol</b></p><ol><li>Uniliteral phonogram for <i>ꜥ</i>.</li><li>Logogram for <i>ꜥ</i> (“arm”).</li></ol></html><h3>Egyptian</h3><p><b>Symbol</b></p><ol><li>Biliteral phonogram for dj used in forms of the verb <i>rdj</i> (“to give”).</li></ol></html><h3>Egyptian</h3><p><b>Symbol</b></p><ol><li>Biliteral phonogram for <b>mj</b>.</li><li>Determinative in <i>jmj</i> (“give&#33;”)</li></ol></html><h3>Egyptian</h3><p><b>Symbol</b></p><ol><li>Biliteral phonogram for <b>nj</b>.</li><li>Ideogram for <i>rmn</i> (“shoulder”).</li><li>Determinative for "arm" and words related to the arm, hand, or actions performed with the arm or hand.</li></ol></html><h3>Egyptian</h3><p><b>Symbol</b></p><ol><li>Determinative in and ideogram for <i>mḥ</i> (“cubit”).</li></ol></html><h3>Egyptian</h3><p><b>Symbol</b></p><ol><li>Biliteral phonogram for <b>ḫw</b>.</li></ol></html><h3>Egyptian</h3><p><b>Symbol</b></p><ol><li>Determinative in and ideogram for <i>ḫrp</i> (“to manage”).</li></ol></html><h3>Egyptian</h3><p><b>Symbol</b></p><ol><li>Determinative in and ideogram for <i>ḏsr</i> (“sacred&#59; to raise the arm”).</li></ol></html><h3>Egyptian</h3><p><b>Symbol</b></p><ol><li>Uniliteral phonogram for <i>d</i>.</li><li>Logogram for <i>ḏrt</i> (“hand”).</li></ol></html><h3>Egyptian</h3><p><b>Symbol</b></p><ol><li>Determinative for "male", such as in <i>ꜥꜣ</i> (“ass”), <i>ṯꜣy</i> (“male, man”), and <i>kꜣ</i> (“bull”).</li><li>Phonetic <i>mt</i>, such as in <i>mtwt</i> (“poison”) and <i>ḫmt</i> 