</td></tr></table>). &lsqb;chiefly Old Kingdom and Late Period&rsqb;</li></ol></html><h3>Egyptian</h3><p><b>Symbol</b></p><ol><li>Determinative in <i>bjk</i> (“falcon”).</li></ol></html><h3>Egyptian</h3><p><b>Symbol</b></p><ol><li>Biliteral phonogram for mt.</li><li>Triliteral phonogram for mjt and mwt.</li><li>Determinative in the word nrt (“vulture”) and words containing nr.</li></ol></html><h3>Egyptian</h3><p><b>Symbol</b></p><ol><li>Uniliteral phonogram for <i>m</i>.</li></ol></html><h3>Egyptian</h3><p><b>Symbol</b></p><ol><li>Biliteral phonogram for <i>mm</i>, as in the preposition <i>mm</i> (“among”).</li><li>Logogram for <i>jm</i> (“therein”). &lsqb;18th Dynasty&rsqb;</li></ol></html><h3>Egyptian</h3><p><b>Symbol</b></p><ol><li>Biliteral phonogram for nḥ.</li><li>Ideogram for nḥ (“guinea fowl”).</li></ol></html><h3>Egyptian</h3><p><b>Symbol</b></p><ol><li>Biliteral phonogram for ḏb and db.</li></ol></html><h3>Egyptian</h3><p><b>Symbol</b></p><ol><li>Determinative in and ideogram for rḫyt (“subjects”).</li></ol></html><h3>Egyptian</h3><p><b>Symbol</b></p><ol><li>Biliteral phonogram for ꜣḫ.</li></ol></html><h3>Egyptian</h3><p><b>Symbol</b></p><ol><li>Triliteral phonogram for <i>dšr</i> (“red”).</li><li>Determinative used in <i>dšr</i> (“flamingo, red”).</li></ol></html><h3>Egyptian</h3><p><b>Symbol</b></p><ol><li>Biliteral phonogram for <i>gm</i>.</li></ol></html><h3>Egyptian</h3><p><b>Symbol</b></p><ol><li>Biliteral phonogram for <i>bꜣ</i>.</li><li>Logogram for <i>bꜣ</i> (“ba”).</li></ol></html><h3>Egyptian</h3><p><b>Symbol</b></p><ol><li>Plural of 𓅡 (bꜣ).</li><li>Ideogram for bꜣw (“impressiveness, power”).</li></ol></html><h3>Egyptian</h3><p><b>Symbol</b></p><ol><li>Determinative for heron.</li></ol></html><h3>Egyptian</h3><p><b>Symbol</b></p><ol><li>Determinative in and ideogram for bꜥḥj (“to flood”).</li></ol></html><h3>Egyptian</h3><p><b>Symbol</b></p><ol><li>A determinative used in sdꜣ (“tremble”).</li></ol></html><h3>Egyptian</h3><p><b>Symbol</b></p><ol><li>A determinative used in njw (“ostrich”).</li></ol></html><h3>Egyptian</h3><p><b>Symbol</b></p><ol><li>Biliteral phonogram for <b>ꜥq</b>.</li></ol></html><h3>Egyptian</h3><p><b>Symbol</b></p><ol><li>Biliteral phonogram for <i>wr</i>, including in the word <i>wr</i>.</li></ol></html><h3>Egyptian</h3><p><b>Symbol</b></p><ol><li>Biliteral phonogram for <i>gb</i>.</li><li>Logogram for <i>ꜣpd</i> (“bird”).</li><li>Determinative for kinds of waterfowl, as in <i>ꜣpd</i>, <i>rꜣ</i>, <i>ṯrp</i>, <i>gbb</i>.</li><li>(<i>in hieratic texts</i>) Determinative for birds and insects in general.</li><li>Phonetic determinative in various verbs&#58; <i>wfꜣ</i> (“to discuss”), <i>wzf</i> (“to be(come) idle”), <i>wdfj</i> (“to be(come) late”), <i>ḥtm</i> (“to perish”).</li></ol></html><h3>Egyptian</h3><p><b>Symbol</b></p><ol><li>Biliteral phonogram for zꜣ.</li><li>Determinative in zr&#47;zrt&#47;zj&#47;zjt (“pintail duck”)</li></ol></html><h3>Egyptian</h3><p><b>Symbol</b></p><ol><li>Biliteral phonogram for pꜣ.</li></ol></html><h3>Egyptian</h3><p><b>Symbol</b></p><ol><li>Biliteral phonogram for pꜣ, used especially in hieratic.</li><li>Determinative in&#58; ḫnj (“to land, alight”) and various other words containing <i>ḫn</i>&#59; sḥwj (“to gather”)&#59; qmyt (“gum”)&#59; qmꜣ (“to throw”)&#59; qmꜣj (“to create”)&#59; and words containing tn and ṯn.</li></ol></html><h3>Egyptian</h3><p><b>Symbol</b></p><ol><li>Determinative in and ideogram for wšꜣ (“to fatten”).</li><li>Determinative in ḏfꜣw (“food”).</li></ol></html><h3>Egyptian</h3><p><b>Symbol</b></p><ol><li>Uniliteral phonogram for <i>w</i>, as in the plural ending <i>-w</i>.</li></ol></html><h3>Egyptian</h3><p><b>Symbol</b></p><ol><li>Biliteral phonogram for ww.</li></ol></html><h3>Egyptian</h3><p><b>Symbol</b></p><ol><li>Bilitieral phonogram for <i>ꜥw</i>.</li></ol></html><h3>Egyptian</h3><p><b>Symbol</b></p><ol><li>Triliteral phonogram for <i>mꜣw</i>.</li></ol></html><h3>Egyptian</h3><p><b>Symbol</b></p><ol><li>Biliteral phonogram for ṯꜣ.</li><li>Ideogram for ṯꜣ (“duckling, chick”).</li></ol></html><h3>Egyptian</h3><p><b>Symbol</b></p><ol><li>Determinative in and ideograph for zš (“nest”).</li></ol></html><h3>Egyptian</h3><p><b>Symbol</b></p><ol><li>Determinative in and ideograph for zš (“nest”).</li></ol></html><h3>Egyptian</h3><p><b>Symbol</b></p><ol><li>Used as an ideogram for rḥtj (“washerman”).</li></ol></html><h3>Egyptian</h3><p><b>Symbol</b></p><ol><li>Determinative in the word ḥꜣm&#47;ḥjm (“to net fish or birds”).</li></ol></html><h3>Egyptian</h3><p><b>Symbol</b></p><ol><li>Determinative in the word snm (“to feed”).</li></ol></html><h3>Egyptian</h3><p><b>Symbol</b></p><ol><li>Ideogram for bꜣ (“ba”, part of the soul).</li></ol></html><h3>Egyptian</h3><p><b>Symbol</b></p><ol><li>Triliteral phonogram for snḏ&#47;snd.</li><li>Determinative in wšn (“to wring the neck of”).</li></ol></html><h3>Egyptian</h3><p><b>Symbol</b></p><ol><li>Logogram for <i>ꜣpdw</i> (“fowl”) in the offering formula.</li><li>Determinative in <i>wšn</i> (“wring the neck of (a bird), offer”).</li><li>(<i>in hieratic texts</i>) Phonetic determinative for <i>mꜣꜥ</i>, by conflation with <table class="mw-hiero-table mw-hiero-outer" dir="ltr" style=" border: 0; border-spacing: 0; font-size:1em;"><tr><td style="padding: 0; text-align: center; vertical-align: middle; font-size:1em;">
