</td></tr></table>).</li></ol></html><h3>Egyptian</h3><p><b>Symbol</b></p><ol><li>Biliteral phonogram for <i>wꜥ</i>, including in the word <i>wꜥ</i>.</li></ol></html><h3>Egyptian</h3><p><b>Symbol</b></p><ol><li>Biliteral phonogram for sn.</li><li>Determinative in the word mꜥbꜣ (“spear”).</li><li>Ideogram for the numeral mꜥbꜣ (“30”).</li></ol></html><h3>Egyptian</h3><p><b>Symbol</b></p><ol><li>Biliteral phonogram for ẖr.</li></ol></html><h3>Egyptian</h3><p><b>Symbol</b></p><ol><li>Ideogram for cutting, used in <i>šꜥ</i>, as well as <i>jw</i>, <i>smꜣ</i>, <i>zfṯ</i>, <i>zft</i>, etc.</li></ol></html><h3>Egyptian</h3><p><b>Symbol</b></p><ol><li>Biliteral phonogram for nm.</li><li>Determinative in the word nm (“butcher knife”).</li></ol></html><h3>Egyptian</h3><p><b>Symbol</b></p><ol><li>Variant of the sign 𓌰 (<table class="mw-hiero-table mw-hiero-outer" dir="ltr" style=" border: 0; border-spacing: 0; font-size:1em;"><tr><td style="padding: 0; text-align: center; vertical-align: middle; font-size:1em;">
