</td></tr></table>), used as a biliteral phonogram for <b>nm</b>.</li></ol></html><h3>Egyptian</h3><p><b>Symbol</b></p><ol><li>Biliteral phonogram for <i>mꜣ</i>.</li><li>Logogram for <i>mꜣ</i> (“stern”).</li><li>Determinative for reap, crooked.</li></ol></html><h3>Egyptian</h3><p><b>Symbol</b></p><ol><li>Biliteral phonogram for mr.</li><li>Determinative for "hack".</li></ol></html><h3>Egyptian</h3><p><b>Symbol</b></p><ol><li>Biliteral phonogram for mr.</li><li>Determinative for "hack".</li></ol></html><h3>Egyptian</h3><p><b>Symbol</b></p><ol><li>Biliteral phonogram for ḥn, based on the word <i>ḥnn</i> (“hoe”).</li></ol></html><h3>Egyptian</h3><p><b>Symbol</b></p><ol><li>Biliteral phonogram for <b>hb</b>.</li><li>Triliteral phonogram for <b>šnꜥ</b>.</li><li>Ideogram for <i>prt</i> (“seed”).</li><li>Determinative for "plow".</li></ol></html><h3>Egyptian</h3><p><b>Symbol</b></p><ol><li>Biliteral phonogram for <i>tm</i>.</li></ol></html><h3>Egyptian</h3><p><b>Symbol</b></p><ol><li>Triliteral phonogram for <b>grg</b>.</li></ol></html><h3>Egyptian</h3><p><b>Symbol</b></p><ol><li>Older variant of the sign 𓍅 (<table class="mw-hiero-table mw-hiero-outer" dir="ltr" style=" border: 0; border-spacing: 0; font-size:1em;"><tr><td style="padding: 0; text-align: center; vertical-align: middle; font-size:1em;">
