</td></tr></table>)</li></ol></html><h3>Egyptian</h3><p><b>Symbol</b></p><ol><li>Triliteral phonogram for <b>stp</b> and <b>sṯp</b>.</li></ol></html><h3>Egyptian</h3><p><b>Symbol</b></p><ol><li>Biliteral phonogram for ꜣb and mr.</li></ol></html><h3>Egyptian</h3><p><b>Symbol</b></p><ol><li>Biliteral phonogram for ḏꜣ.</li><li>Used as an abbreviation of <i>wḏꜣ</i> (“to be in good condition”) in the honorific <i>ꜥnḫ wḏꜣ snb</i>.</li></ol></html><h3>Egyptian</h3><p><b>Symbol</b></p><ol><li>Biliteral phonogram for ḏꜣ.</li></ol></html><h3>Egyptian</h3><p><b>Symbol</b></p><ol><li>Biliteral phonogram for <i>tꜣ</i>.</li></ol></html><h3>Egyptian</h3><p><b>Symbol</b></p><ol><li>Biliteral phonogram for tj.</li><li>Uniliteral phonogram for t.</li></ol></html><h3>Egyptian</h3><p><b>Symbol</b></p><ol><li>Biliteral phonogram for <b>ḥm</b>.</li></ol></html><h3>Egyptian</h3><p><b>Symbol</b></p><ol><li>Determinative in the word <i>ẖꜥq</i> (“to shave”).</li></ol></html><h3>Egyptian</h3><p><b>Symbol</b></p><ol><li>Biliteral phonogram for <b>šn</b> in the word <i>šnt</i> (“dispute”).</li><li>Ideogram for <i>št</i> (“100”).</li><li>Determinative for "rope," "tie," and "coil".</li></ol></html><h3>Egyptian</h3><p><b>Symbol</b></p><ol><li>Biliteral phonogram for wꜣ.</li></ol></html><h3>Egyptian</h3><p><b>Symbol</b></p><ol><li>Ideogram for and determinative in the word <i>snṯj</i> (“design”).</li></ol></html><h3>Egyptian</h3><p><b>Symbol</b></p><ol><li>Biliteral phonogram for <b>šs</b>.</li><li>Triliteral phonogram for <b>šsr</b>.</li><li>Ideogram for <i>šsrw</i>&#47;<i>šs</i> (“linen”).</li></ol></html><h3>Egyptian</h3><p><b>Symbol</b></p><ol><li>Biliteral phonogram for <b>šn</b>.</li></ol></html><h3>Egyptian</h3><p><b>Symbol</b></p><ol><li>Used in transcribing hieratic signs into hieroglyphs in cases where it is not clear whether a given hieratic sign represents <table class="mw-hiero-table mw-hiero-outer" dir="ltr" style=" border: 0; border-spacing: 0; font-size:1em;"><tr><td style="padding