</td></tr></table> (<i>sn</i>). See <i>𓍲</i> or <i>𓌢</i> for usage.</li></ol></html><h3>Egyptian</h3><p><b>Symbol</b></p><ol><li>Logogram for <i>šnw</i> (“cartouche”).</li><li>Determinative in words for the cartouche, as in <i>šnw</i>.</li></ol></html><h3>Egyptian</h3><p><b>Symbol</b></p><ol><li>Uniliteral phonogram for <i>ṯ</i>&#59; since Middle Egyptian sometimes used for <i>t</i>, as the sounds had merged in some phonetic environments.</li></ol></html><h3>Egyptian</h3><p><b>Symbol</b></p><ol><li>Biliteral phonogram for <b>jṯ</b> and <b>jt</b>.</li></ol></html><h3>Egyptian</h3><p><b>Symbol</b></p><ol><li>Biliteral phonogram for <b>zꜣ</b>.</li></ol></html><h3>Egyptian</h3><p><b>Symbol</b></p><ol><li>Biliteral phonogram for <b>zꜣ</b>.</li></ol></html><h3>Egyptian</h3><p><b>Symbol</b></p><ol><li>Biliteral phonogram for <b>ꜥḏ</b> and <b>ꜥd</b>.</li><li>Determinative in and ideogram for ꜥḏ (“reel”).</li></ol></html><h3>Egyptian</h3><p><b>Symbol</b></p><ol><li>Uniliteral phonogram for <i>ḥ</i>.</li><li>(<i>rare</i>) Determinative in <i>tkꜣw</i> (“candle, taper”).</li></ol></html><h3>Egyptian</h3><p><b>Symbol</b></p><ol><li>Biliteral phonogram for <b>sk</b>.</li><li>Biliteral phonogram for <b>wꜣḥ</b>.</li><li>Determinative in the word ḫsr (“to ward off”).</li><li>Sometimes used in place of 𓆭 (<table class="mw-hiero-table mw-hiero-outer" dir="ltr" style=" border: 0; border-spacing: 0; font-size:1em;"><tr><td style="padding: 0; text-align: center; vertical-align: middle; font-size:1em;">
