</td></tr></table>) in <b>mꜥr (“fortunate”)</b>.</li></ol></html><h3>Egyptian</h3><p><b>Symbol</b></p><ol><li>Biliteral phonogram for <i>nb</i>.</li></ol></html><h3>Egyptian</h3><p><b>Symbol</b></p><ol><li>Uniliteral phonogram for <i>k</i>.</li></ol></html><h3>Egyptian</h3><p><b>Symbol</b></p><ol><li>alternative form of <i>𓎡</i></li></ol></html><h3>Egyptian</h3><p><b>Symbol</b></p><ol><li>Biliteral phonogram for ḥn.</li></ol></html><h3>Egyptian</h3><p><b>Symbol</b></p><ol><li>Determinative for oil and unguent.</li><li>alternative form of <i>𓎰</i> (<table class="mw-hiero-table mw-hiero-outer" dir="ltr" style=" border: 0; border-spacing: 0; font-size:1em;"><tr><td style="padding: 0; text-align: center; vertical-align: middle; font-size:1em;">
