</td></tr></table>). &lsqb;since the Middle Kingdom&rsqb;</li></ol></html><h3>Egyptian</h3><p><b>Symbol</b></p><ol><li>Triliteral phonogram for <i>bꜣs</i>, as in <i>bꜣstt</i> (“(cat-goddess) Bastet”).</li><li>Determinative for jar, as in <i>bꜣs</i> (“jar”).</li></ol></html><h3>Egyptian</h3><p><b>Symbol</b></p><ol><li>Determinative for alabaster, as in <i>šs</i> (“alabaster”).</li><li>Logogram for <i>ḥꜣb</i> (“feast”).</li><li>Phonogram for <i>ḥꜣb</i>, as in <i>ḥꜣbj</i> (“to mourn”).</li><li>Determinative for feast, as in <i>psḏntjw</i> (“new-moon festival”), <i>wꜣg</i> (“wag-festival”).</li></ol></html><h3>Egyptian</h3><p><b>Symbol</b></p><ol><li>Uniliteral phonogram for <i>g</i>.</li><li>Logogram for or determinative in <i>nst</i> (“throne”).</li><li>Logogram for or determinative in <i>dšrt</i> (“red pot”), by conflation with <table class="mw-hiero-table mw-hiero-outer" dir="ltr" style=" border: 0; border-spacing: 0; font-size:1em;"><tr><td style="padding: 0; text-align: center; vertical-align: middle; font-size:1em;">
