</td></tr></table> (<i>𓊒</i>). &lsqb;18th Dynasty&rsqb;</li></ol></html><h3>Egyptian</h3><p><b>Symbol</b></p><ol><li>alternative form of <i>𓎼</i></li></ol></html><h3>Egyptian</h3><p><b>Symbol</b></p><ol><li>Determinative in and ideogram for the word <i>dšrt</i> (“redware”).</li></ol></html><h3>Egyptian</h3><p><b>Symbol</b></p><ol><li>Biliteral phonogram for <b>ḥs</b> and ḥz.</li><li>Determinative in the word <i>ḥzt</i> (“water jar”).</li><li>Determinative in and ideogram for the word <i>snbt</i> (“jar”).</li></ol></html><h3>Egyptian</h3><p><b>Symbol</b></p><ol><li>Logogram for <i>ḫnt</i> (“jar-stand”).</li><li>Phonogram for <i>ḫnt</i>.</li></ol></html><h3>Egyptian</h3><p><b>Symbol</b></p><ol><li>Logogram for <i>ḫnt</i> (“jar-stand”). &lsqb;Old Kingdom&rsqb;</li><li>Phonogram for <i>ḫnt</i>. &lsqb;Old Kingdom&rsqb;</li></ol></html><h3>Egyptian</h3><p><b>Symbol</b></p><ol><li>Biliteral phonogram for mj.</li><li>Determinative in the word mhr (“milk jug”).</li></ol></html><h3>Egyptian</h3><p><b>Symbol</b></p><ol><li>Phonogram for <i>nw</i>.</li><li>Phonogram for <i>jn</i>, as in <i>jnk</i> (“I”).</li><li>Phonetic determinative for <i>ḏꜣḏꜣ</i>, as in <i>ḏꜣḏꜣt</i> (“council”).</li><li>Phonetic determinative for <i>qd</i>, as in <i>qd</i> (“to build”). &lsqb;since the Middle Kingdom&rsqb;</li><li>Phonetic determinative for <i>nḏ</i>, as in <i>nḏ</i> (“to protect”). &lsqb;since the Middle Kingdom&rsqb;</li><li>Phonetic determinative for <i>nḫb</i>, as in <i>nḫbt</i> (“Nekhbet”).</li><li>Part of the combination <table class="mw-hiero-table mw-hiero-outer" dir="ltr" style=" border: 0; border-spacing: 0; font-size:1em;"><tr><td style="padding: 0; text-align: center; vertical-align: middle; font-size:1em;">
