</td></tr></table> (<i>𓏋</i>).</li></ol></html><h3>Egyptian</h3><p><b>Symbol</b></p><ol><li>Uniliteral phonogram for <i>t</i>.</li><li>Logogram for <i>t</i> (“bread”).</li><li>Logogram for <i>jt</i> (“father”) in <i>jt-nṯr</i> (a type of priest, literally “god’s father”).</li></ol></html><h3>Egyptian</h3><p><b>Symbol</b></p><ol><li>Ideogram for <i>rḏj, ḏj</i> (“give”).</li></ol></html><h3>Egyptian</h3><p><b>Symbol</b></p><ol><li>Logogram for <i>mḏꜣt</i> (“book”). &lsqb;since the 12th Dynasty&rsqb;</li><li>Phonogram for <i>mḏꜣt</i>. &lsqb;since the 12th Dynasty&rsqb;</li><li>Determinative for writing and written things, as in <i>zẖꜣ</i> (“to write”), <i>mdwt</i> (“words”). &lsqb;since the 12th Dynasty&rsqb;</li><li>Determinative for abstract notions, as in <i>mꜣꜥt</i> (“truth”), <i>rḫ</i> (“to know”). &lsqb;since the 12th Dynasty&rsqb;</li><li>Logogram for <i>dmḏ</i> (“total”) (in mathematical books and accounts). &lsqb;since the 12th Dynasty&rsqb;</li></ol></html><h3>Egyptian</h3><p><b>Symbol</b></p><ol><li>alternative form of <i>𓏛</i></li></ol></html><h3>Egyptian</h3><p><b>Symbol</b></p><ol><li>Logogram for <i>mḏꜣt</i> (“book”). &lsqb;Old Kingdom&rsqb;</li><li>Phonogram for <i>mḏꜣt</i>. &lsqb;Old Kingdom&rsqb;</li><li>Determinative for writing and written things, as in <i>zẖꜣ</i> (“to write”), <i>mdwt</i> (“words”). &lsqb;Old Kingdom&rsqb;</li><li>Determinative for abstract notions, as in <i>mꜣꜥt</i> (“truth”), <i>rḫ</i> (“to know”). &lsqb;Old Kingdom&rsqb;</li></ol></html><h3>Egyptian</h3><p><b>Symbol</b></p><ol><li>Biliteral phonogram for mn.</li></ol></html><h3>Egyptian</h3><p><b>Symbol</b></p><ol><li>Uniliteral phonogram for <i>j</i>. &lsqb;since the Middle Kingdom&rsqb;</li><li>Logogram for <i>-j</i> (dual ending), originally replacing (for superstitious reasons) the device of writing the determinative twice in certain contexts. &lsqb;since the Pyramid Texts&rsqb;</li><li>Written in place of two difficult-to-draw signs. &lsqb;mostly since the 19th Dynasty&rsqb;</li></ol></html><h3>Egyptian</h3><p><b>Symbol</b></p><ol><li>alternative form of <i>𓅱</i> (<table class="mw-hiero-table mw-hiero-outer" dir="ltr" style=" border: 0; border-spacing: 0; font-size:1em;"><tr><td style="padding: 0; text-align: center; vertical-align: middle; font-size:1em;">
