</td></tr></table>)</li></ol></html><h3>Egyptian</h3><p><b>Symbol</b></p><ol><li>Determinative relating to meanings of break, cross, or number.</li><li>Phonogram for&#58; <i>swꜣ</i> in swꜣj (“pass”)&#59; <i>zwꜣ</i> in zwꜣ (“cut off”)&#59; <i>sḏ</i> in sḏt (“flame”)&#59; <i>šbn</i> in šbn (“mix”) and related words&#59; <i>ḫbs</i> in ḫbsw (“cultivation”)&#59; <i>wp</i> in wp-st (“detail”)&#59; and wr in a few words.</li></ol></html><h3>Egyptian</h3><p><b>Symbol</b></p><ol><li>An older variant of the sign 𓏴, used as a determinative and a phonogram with several different phonetic values.</li></ol></html><h3>Egyptian</h3><p><b>Symbol</b></p><ol><li>Biliteral phonogram for jm.</li><li>Used as a variant of the sign 𓇬, from which it is indistinguishable in hieratic.</li></ol></html><h3>Egyptian</h3><p><b>Symbol</b></p><ol><li>Uniliteral phonogram for <i>ḫ</i>.</li><li>Logogram for <i>ḫ</i> (“placenta<sup>&#63;</sup>, child&#59; to be a child”).</li></ol></html><h3>Egyptian</h3><p><b>Symbol</b></p><ol><li>Logogram for <i>ḥjpt</i> (“course”).</li><li>Biliteral phonogram for <i>ḥp</i>, as in <i>ḥp</i> (“Apis”), <i>ḥpy</i> (“Hapy”), <i>ḥpt</i> (“steering oar”).</li></ol></html><h3>Egyptian</h3><p><b>Symbol</b></p><ol><li>Biliteral phonogram for <b>qn</b>.</li><li>Determinative in and ideogram for <i>spꜣt</i> (“estate”).</li><li>Determinative in <i>ḏꜣḏꜣt</i> (“council”).</li><li>Variant of 𓈈 as an ideogram for <i>spꜣt</i> (“nome”).</li><li>Variant of 𓊃 as a phonogram for <b>z</b> in <i>zmjt</i> (“desert”).</li><li>Variant of 𓎙 as a phonogram for ꜥḏ.</li></ol></html><h3>Egyptian</h3><p><b>Symbol</b></p><ol><li>Triliteral for <i>mꜣꜥ</i>, e.g. for the word <i>mꜣꜥ</i> in <i>mꜣꜥ-ḫrw</i>.</li></ol></html><h3>Egyptian</h3><p><b>Symbol</b></p><ol><li>Biliteral phonogram for jm.</li><li>Uniliteral phonogram for m</li></ol></html><h3>Egyptian</h3><p><b>Symbol</b></p><ol><li>Ideogram for <i>gs</i> (“side, half”).</li><li>Biliteral phonogram for gs.</li></ol></html><h3>Egyptian</h3><p><b>Symbol</b></p><ol><li>Logogram for <i>sꜣ</i> (“back”). &lsqb;Old Kingdom and Middle Kingdom&rsqb;</li><li>Phonogram for <i>sꜣ</i>. &lsqb;Old Kingdom and Middle Kingdom&rsqb;</li></ol></html><h3>Egyptian</h3><p><b>Symbol</b></p><ol><li>Logogram for <i>sꜣ</i> (“back”). &lsqb;since the 12th Dynasty&rsqb;</li><li>Phonogram for <i>sꜣ</i>. &lsqb;since the 12th Dynasty&rsqb;</li><li>(<i>group-writing</i>) The group <table class="mw-hiero-table mw-hiero-outer" dir="ltr" style=" border: 0; border-spacing: 0; font-size:1em;"><tr><td style="padding: 0; text-align: center; vertical-align: middle; font-size:1em;">
